    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s C176A drawing. Its tile corners were snapped to the square-root-of-two grid in small-star-radius units. The unit-star opening is shared with the other Moroccan reconstructions. After it every line, the tile’s sides too, is drawn through a crossing of the star’s sides, carried on, with earlier lines, and turned round O. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The tile edges follow the plain drawing. The colours follow Wichmann’s drawing: red, black and white, in the Modern Moroccan palette. No photograph was checked. Wichmann notes that his drawing omits the panel’s central 24-pointed star; this repeat follows his drawing.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
